# Security headers for the static apex origin (laikacms.com), served by
# Cloudflare Pages. This origin is deliberately cookie-free and static-only —
# the authenticated platform lives on its own origin (app.laikacms.com) so a
# supply-chain compromise of anything built into this site can never reach a
# session. See laika-cloud: decisions/0028 + docs/security/apex-origin-isolation.md.
#
# CSP is defense-in-depth here, not the primary control (that is the absence
# of any secret on this origin). connect-src 'self' still cuts off the easy
# exfiltration channels for injected script.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# VitePress needs an inline theme-preference script in <head> (dark-mode
# flash prevention), so /docs/* relaxes script-src to 'unsafe-inline'.
# It self-hosts its fonts, so the Google Fonts hosts are dropped.
/docs/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data:; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
